{# goal: Synthesize the engagement report — three tracks, defense coverage, MCDA, remediations, hard-stop, convergence. #}
[inference]
template_type: KnowAct
contract:
  input:
    task: string
    seam_map: object
    security_track: object
    arch_track: object
    ui_track: object
    annotated_findings: array
    mcda: object
    applied_remediations: array
    hard_stop: object
    convergence_score: number
    iterations: number
  output:
    report: object
visibility: Public
---
[inference]
temperature = 0.4
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "normal"
max_tokens = 4096
thinking_budget = "full"

You are synthesizing the final engagement report. Task: {{ task }}.

## Inputs

seam_map (divergence surface + prior verdicts + slices):
{{ seam_map }}

security track (findings + defense_layer_coverage):
{{ security_track }}

architecture track (findings + dead_surface_summary):
{{ arch_track }}

ui track (findings + pattern_gap_summary):
{{ ui_track }}

annotated_findings (constraint_force + deletion_test + feedback verdict):
{{ annotated_findings }}

mcda (ranked_remediations + top3 + sensitivity):
{{ mcda }}

applied_remediations:
{{ applied_remediations }}

hard_stop decision:
{{ hard_stop }}

convergence_score: {{ convergence_score }} (count of uncited-or-unadjudicated findings; 0 = clean)
iterations: {{ iterations }}

## Synthesis

Produce a consolidated report with: (1) a verdict (Pass / Conditional / Fail)
derived from the defense-layer coverage + whether any blocking finding remains
unremediated; (2) the count of findings per track and per severity; (3) the
MCDA top-3 and whether `stable_under_perturbation` held; (4) the applied
remediations (with test descriptions) and the hard-stop decision; (5) the
deliverable paths (reports under `kask/research/seam-audit/`, the FlowDef
manifest under `kask/registry/manifests/kask-seam-audit.yaml` + templates under
`kask/registry/templates/kask-seam-audit/`); (6) the convergence score and
iteration count. Cite `file:line` throughout.

## Output (JSON only)

```json
{
  "report": {
    "verdict": "Pass|Conditional|Fail",
    "findings_per_track": { "security": N, "architecture": N, "ui": N },
    "findings_per_severity": { "critical": N, "high": N, "medium": N, "low": N, "info": N },
    "defense_layer_coverage": { "covered": N, "missing": N, "missing_layers": [ ... ] },
    "mcda_top3": [ { "id": "...", "weighted_total": 0.0 } ],
    "mcda_stable_under_perturbation": true,
    "applied_remediations": [ { "id": "...", "test_description": "..." } ],
    "hard_stop_triggered": false,
    "deferred_remediations": [ { "id": "...", "reason": "..." } ],
    "deliverable_paths": {
      "reports": "kask/research/seam-audit/",
      "flowdef_manifest": "kask/registry/manifests/kask-seam-audit.yaml",
      "flowdef_templates": "kask/registry/templates/kask-seam-audit/"
    },
    "convergence_score": 0,
    "iterations": 1
  }
}
```

Do not fabricate. If a track produced no findings, record 0. If remediations
were deferred (not applied in-session), list them in `deferred_remediations`
with the reason (e.g. "requires workspace compile verification exceeding a
safe single-session bound").